# AWS CCP — Billing, Pricing & Support

Which EC2 pricing model has no commitment and bills by the second or hour?
---
On-Demand
~ Reserved Instances
~ Spot Instances
~ Savings Plans
---
The most expensive per hour and the baseline every discount is measured against.

Which pricing option offers the deepest discount, up to 90%, for workloads that tolerate interruption?
---
Spot Instances
~ Reserved Instances
~ Savings Plans
~ Dedicated Hosts
---
AWS can reclaim Spot capacity with a two-minute warning. Great for batch, wrong for databases.

Which pricing model commits to a consistent amount of compute spend per hour for 1 or 3 years, flexible across instance types?
---
Savings Plans
~ Reserved Instances
~ Spot Instances
~ On-Demand
---
Similar discounts to Reserved Instances (up to 72%) with more flexibility.

Which option gives you an entire physical server, often for bring-your-own-license software?
---
Dedicated Hosts
~ Reserved Instances
~ Spot Instances
~ Savings Plans
---
Visibility into sockets and cores for per-socket licensing. The priciest way to run EC2.

Which direction of data transfer is generally free?
---
Inbound to AWS
~ Outbound to the internet
~ Both directions
~ Neither direction
---
Egress is billed. That asymmetry shapes a lot of architectures.

The AWS Free Tier has three offer types: always free, {{12 months}} free, and short-term trials.
---
Lambda's million requests per month never expires. The EC2 750 micro-instance hours end after a year.

Which tool visualizes your historical AWS spend with graphs and forecasts?
---
Cost Explorer
= AWS Cost Explorer
---
Filter by service, account, or tag. Forecasts are based on past usage.

Which service sends an alert when your spend or usage crosses a threshold you set?
---
Budgets
= AWS Budgets
---
Budgets can also alert on Reserved Instance and Savings Plans utilization.

Which billing tool provides the most detailed, line-item usage data?
---
Cost and Usage Report
~ Cost Explorer
~ The billing dashboard
~ Trusted Advisor
---
Delivered to an S3 bucket for analysis with Athena or your own tooling.

Which tool estimates the monthly cost of an architecture before you build it?
---
Pricing Calculator
= AWS Pricing Calculator
---
Shareable estimates per service and Region. It replaced the old Simple Monthly Calculator.

Which service centrally manages multiple AWS accounts and combines their usage into one bill?
---
Organizations
= AWS Organizations
---
Consolidated billing aggregates usage across accounts, so volume discounts kick in sooner.

What do Service Control Policies (SCPs) do?
---
Set the maximum permissions available to accounts in an organization
~ Grant permissions to IAM users
~ Encrypt data shared between accounts
~ Split one bill across accounts
---
SCPs never grant anything. They are guardrails that cap what account admins can allow.

Cost allocation {{tags}} let you break the bill down by project, team, or environment.
---
Activate them in the billing console or they never show up in Cost Explorer.

Which support plan is included free with every AWS account?
---
Basic
~ Developer
~ Business
~ Enterprise
---
Account and billing help plus documentation. No technical support cases.

Which is the cheapest support plan with 24/7 phone and chat access to engineers?
---
Business
~ Developer
~ Basic
~ Enterprise On-Ramp
---
Developer is business-hours email only. Business also unlocks full Trusted Advisor checks.

Which support plan includes a designated Technical Account Manager?
---
Enterprise
~ Business
~ Enterprise On-Ramp
~ Developer
---
Enterprise On-Ramp offers a pool of TAMs. Enterprise assigns you your own.

On the Enterprise support plan, business-critical outages get a response within {{15}} minutes.
---
Business plan promises 1 hour for production down, Enterprise On-Ramp 30 minutes for business-critical.

Which tool checks your account against best practices for cost, performance, security, fault tolerance, and service quotas?
---
Trusted Advisor
= AWS Trusted Advisor
---
Everyone gets the core security checks. The full set needs Business support or higher.

Where do you buy third-party software preconfigured to run on AWS?
---
Marketplace
= AWS Marketplace
---
Charges land on your AWS bill. Many listings bill by the hour like the infrastructure under them.
